{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/529324-what-is-an-interesting-limited-hedge-resource","id":529324,"title":"What is an interesting limited hedge resource?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-26T15:29:54-07:00","id":529324,"title":"What is an interesting limited hedge resource?","content":"My goal for my new campaign is to give it a wild west feel. In that vein, I am trying to think of a good hedge resource that would work as a sort of changeling boomtown. Maybe a proliferation of goblin fruit or something. What kind of item do you think would make a good gold rush changeling item?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:28:54-07:00","id":529389,"title":"","content":"Do you want a specific Court to dominate the town? If your players are Summer, the given item could be useful in combat. A luxury item that's beautiful or fragrant falls more under Spring's banner. (Of course, given the greed that town must radiate, maybe they'd rule it anyway...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:19:57-07:00","id":529422,"title":"","content":"There are Goblin Miners in... I want to say Dancers in the Dusk? Anyway, they could be pretty good inspiration. They build tunnels in the Hedge that lead into the dreams of mortals, from which they mine valuable &quot;jewels&quot;. You'd probably need to have some fairly amoral Changelings if you wanted them operating in exactly that fashion, but there are ways around that. Maybe they find abandoned mine shafts and aren't aware of where those mines lead? The Changelings only begin to realise the consequences of their actions as the shafts begin to run &quot;dry&quot; and they notice mortals beginning to behave oddly in the real world as a consequence.<br /> <br /> A correctly themed Goblin Market operating in the area would help accentuate the boomtown feel, I think. Good place to trade those jewels for items of more immediate use to the Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T21:54:32-07:00","id":531731,"title":"","content":"Couple ideas:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Phantasos</b></u> - An ore found within stone in the Hedge. It is indistinguishable from normal stone except by moonlight. Special lanterns filled with captured moonlight are used to mine the ore. When properly alloyed and forged it can be fashioned into items which counter fae magics. (Items provide a bonus both to rolls to resist Contracts and to resistance traits used as passive resistance to Contracts.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Midnight Oil</b></u> - A highly reflective viscous black liquid found in underground reserves in the Hedge. It must be drilled for and pumped like crude oil. When burned in a hedgespun furnace or lamp, the oil radiates glamour which can be gleaned by nearby Changelings. (Roughly 1 per 1/2 ounce in a lamp, which takes an hour to burn. More from a furnace, which would be suitable as a Hollow feature for a Motley.) It may only be burned at night; daytime renders it inert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}